  "verdict": "no_source_outside_the_family_names_these_faces_but_five_directory_censuses_read_every_published_face_and_one_of_them_carries_a_published_verdict_forward",
  "reasons": [
    "of the 13 names only the family writes at this pin, 0 is loaded by a source outside the family; the 0 non-family occurrence(s) are literals that are compared or printed, never opened -- a name census reports zero readers and that is a statement about writers",
    "the population moved since E341: 2 of its 15 names gained a namer outside the family and 0 of them gained a loader -- the drift is published rather than absorbed into a smaller population",
    "5 directory census(es) read every published face in results/state_tilt without naming it, so 13 of the 13 names have a reader and 0 has none",
    "what those readers take is uneven and published per reader: carries=1 | declarations=1 | envelope_only=1 | measures_shape=2",
    "the family's numbers do not gate anything outside it: one reader copies a `verdict` into its own row and the rest take leaf paths, stamps or declared lists -- so these faces are population members of a census of censuses rather than inputs to a decision"
  ],
  "limits": {
    "class_is_cited_not_proved": "what each reader takes is a frozen evidence row with quoted code re-checked at the pin, not a dataflow proof: a comparison against a face value inside a helper this study does not follow would not be seen",
    "admission_is_pattern_matching": "a census that enumerates results and then filters by a name rule *after* the load is admitted here, which is the reading its own docstring takes",
    "literals_are_not_paths": "a literal that reaches `open` is a load even when the path is assembled elsewhere; the reading is deliberately wider than 'this file opened this face' and is stated as such",
    "pinned_commit": "the corpus and every face are read at 90c1fa8ae; this file lands after it, so it is one .py smaller than the tree that publishes this face"
  }
}
